# Breaking Down the Generate and Judge Guide

In the previous level, you explored an example Generate and Judge Guide created by a student. This level breaks down the major sections of the project and highlights how students apply the big ideas from across the unit.

As you review each section, notice how the student moves beyond simple reactions about AI and instead makes evidence-based judgments about responsible AI use.

## Opening Section

<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:25px 0px;">
<tr>
<td style="width:40%; vertical-align:top; padding-right:20px;">

This opening section introduces the topic, audience, and purpose of the guide.

By choosing a specific audience and focus, the student creates a clearer foundation for the project.

</td>
<td style="width:60%; vertical-align:top;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/754c6f55e839f235de4e6d183363ffb6-image-1779395945932.32.01 PM.png" alt="Audience, theme, and purpose of the AI Guide" style="width:100%; border-radius:10px;">
</td>
</tr>
</table>

<div style="border-top: 1px solid #048899; margin: 30px 0px;"></div>

## Helpful vs. Unhelpful AI Use

<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:25px 0px;">
<tr>
<td style="width:40%; vertical-align:top; padding-right:20px;">

This section helps students compare responsible and irresponsible uses of AI.

The student explains both the benefits and risks while emphasizing that humans are responsible for what gets shared.

</td>
<td style="width:60%; vertical-align:top;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/7fc29fcb8841d9137ac5dc2ed778d407-image-1779396005869.32.34 PM.png" alt="Chat examples of helpful and unhelpful AI use" style="width:100%; border-radius:10px;">
</td>
</tr>
</table>

<div style="border-top: 1px solid #048899; margin: 30px 0px;"></div>

## Chatbot Evidence

<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:25px 0px;">
<tr>
<td style="width:40%; vertical-align:top; padding-right:20px;">

This section gives students the opportunity to test and evaluate AI-generated responses.

The student analyzes the chatbot’s output, identifies strengths and weaknesses, and explains why human judgment is still necessary.

</td>
<td style="width:60%; vertical-align:top;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/64e5c35389ecbd6817a9e7c6c004fc8f-image-1779396005828.32.57 PM.png" alt="Logs of custom chatbot use" style="width:100%; border-radius:10px;">
</td>
</tr>
</table>

<div style="border-top: 1px solid #048899; margin: 30px 0px;"></div>

## Image Generation

<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:25px 0px;">
<tr>
<td style="width:40%; vertical-align:top; padding-right:20px;">

This section encourages students to think critically about AI-generated images and misinformation.

The student reflects on audience trust, realism, and the responsibility creators have when sharing AI-generated media.

</td>
<td style="width:60%; vertical-align:top;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/8daca8f013fe688c80bcfbfccaf54f0a-image-1779396005857.32.47 PM.png" alt="A generated image and tips for image gen" style="width:100%; border-radius:10px;">
</td>
</tr>
</table>

<div style="border-top: 1px solid #048899; margin: 30px 0px;"></div>

## Tips for Responsible Use

<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:25px 0px;">
<tr>
<td style="width:40%; vertical-align:top; padding-right:20px;">

This final section synthesizes ideas from across the unit into practical advice for others.
  
The student connects recommendations back to earlier investigations and demonstrates evidence-based reasoning about AI use.

</td>
<td style="width:60%; vertical-align:top;">
